  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>At 42 rue Thiers, steps from the seafront and the old port of Saint-Raphaël, Moelleuses & Persillées serves French-Italian bistronomic cuisine centred on aged meats (Black Angus, Wagyu, Kobe), in a cosy setting with an air-conditioned dining room and air-conditioned indoor and outdoor terraces. The official website (mpstraphael.fr) states that the restaurant "accepts dogs" and welcomes children.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Hours published on the official website from 31 August: Monday and Tuesday evenings (7pm-10:30pm), Thursday, Friday and Sunday lunch (12pm-2:30pm) and evening, Saturday evening only; closed Wednesday. Book on 04 69 00 21 60 or reservation@mpstraphael.fr. Adaptable menu (vegetarian options), parking nearby. The website does not say whether dogs are admitted in the dining room or only on the terrace, nor the accepted size or water bowl: ask when booking.</p>
      <p>Worth checking before you go: the listing previously gave a different phone number and 7-days-a-week opening, which no longer appear on the official website. Source: mpstraphael.fr (home page), read on 06/11/2026.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: if you're travelling with a good appetite and a well-behaved dog under the table, this is one of the best addresses in the area for meat.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The old port of Saint-Raphaël is right nearby, pleasant for a walk before or after the meal.</p>
